This is a great question! It addresses a core architectural decision.

Here is the best practice for your system design to avoid conflicts and keep your data clean:

1. Where to put Insurance Companies?
✅ Correct Place: apps/crm/models/partner.py (Model: Partner)

Why? Partner is designed for entities that pay on behalf of customers (Insurance, BNPL, Companies).
Fields: It has fields like credit_limit, payment_terms, and partner_type='insurance', which are exactly what you need for an insurance company.
❌ Wrong Place: apps/crm/models/customer.py (Model: Customer)

Why? Customer is designed for the person receiving the service (the patient).
But what about company type in Customer? This is only used if you are selling goods directly to a company for their own use (e.g., selling 50 safety goggles to a construction firm). It is NOT for insurance coverage.
2. How to handle "Many Insurance Companies"?
You do NOT need to create a separate InvoiceType for every single insurance company (e.g., "Invoice AXA", "Invoice BUPA", "Invoice Tawuniya"). That is unmanageable.

The Recommended Flow:

Create 1 Invoice Type:
Name: "Insurance Claim" (or "Credit Sales").
Pricing Policy: Link it to a general "Insurance Pricing Policy".
Add Insurance Companies as Partners:
Go to Partners menu.
Add "BUPA" (Type: Insurance).
Add "Tawuniya" (Type: Insurance).
The "Magic" Link (Flexible Pricing):
Go to Flexible Prices.
Create a price rule.
Select Pricing Policy: "Insurance Pricing Policy".
Select Partner: "BUPA".
Now this price only applies when the invoice type is "Insurance Claim" AND the selected partner is "BUPA".
Summary Table
Concept	Model	Example Data	Function
Who wears the glasses?	Customer	"John Doe"	Medical records, Prescription
Who pays the bill?	Partner	"BUPA Insurance"	Credit Limit, Contracts, Claims
What is the transaction?	InvoiceType	"Insurance Invoice"	GL Accounts, General Pricing Policy
How much does it cost?	FlexiblePrice	"BUPA Frame Price"	Specific price for BUPA
Conclusion: Keep Customer for individuals (patients). Use Partner for all your insurance companies. This design is conflict-free and scalable!